  "notes": "Governmental activities are cash basis (net position = cash: cash and investments 10,274,841 + county treasurer 134,394 = 10,409,235); business-type activities are accrual (net position). No governmental funds statement is in the trimmed PDF, so governmental receipts/disbursements come from the Statement of Activities (p2): program revenues by function and column plus general revenues; disbursements by function. Governmental receipts total 12,424,738 = disbursements 13,505,719 + change in net position (1,080,981). Beginning cash = beginning net position 11,490,216 (no restatement for governmental). No transfers appear in the government-wide statement (business-type general revenues 503,461 = investment 381,901 + miscellaneous 121,560, which is lease income on the REN statement p4). Fund-level transfers on budget schedules (pp6-8) are internal and eliminated, so top-level transfers are null; they are listed in detail as other financing. Public buildings and facilities mapped to general government. Business-type: REN statement p4 for receipts/expenses (interest expense 22,757 treated as a disbursement); capital contributions 320,205 offset by plant cost recovered (320,205) net to zero; restatement (156,799) as business_type adjustment; beginning 57,374,820 is as previously reported. Business-type balance 55,334,284 reconciles: 57,374,820 - 156,799 - 1,883,737. Balance sheet uses government-wide Statement of Net Position, Total column (p1). Compensated absences long-term portion categorized other liabilities. Detail: only budget schedules for General, Street Department, Economic Development funds and LB840 schedule (p9) are in the trimmed PDF. LB840 schedule may overlap the Economic Development fund (program income 87,294 vs 91,669; different figures), recorded separately and flagged; its 'Sales tax transfer from City' recorded as other financing and included in the printed revenue total. Grant income categorized federal grants with review since source is not stated. Read pages 1-9 of 9 LB840 Funds schedule (p9) left out of detail: it is a subset of the Economic Development Fund schedule (p8) (same 347,521 transfer and 9,139 interest; program income and spending inside the ED lines), so recording both would double count. Charges for Services - General government 225,749 categorized licenses and permits (equals GF Licenses and permits, p6). GF grant/contribution lines on p2 include GF Donations 130,956 (p6); kept under grants as the dominant part, with review."
